{1 Memory management}

TODO: cover
- The OCaml GC owns every value; there is no [unref] or [free] to call.
  Docs translated from C drop "free the result with ..." sentences for
  this reason.
- What keeps a widget alive (its parent container, a window, your
  reference).
- Anything that does need explicit cleanup (check: for example closing
  streams, destroying windows).

